// A mixed Int/Float equality in a PROVIDE-METHOD body (issue #2715 review).
//
// The component stratum has its own python renderer: `_ComponentEmitter._expr`
// in the reference, `cexpr` in selfhost/emit_py.rvl. Both are distinct from the
// module-fn `_expr`, which already read the frontend's `"widen": "Float"`
// marker on the operand of `x == 4.0`. Nothing in the corpus reached the
// COMPONENT renderer's widen branch, so the statement ledger recorded it as
// newly uncovered (40 -> 42), and the self-host `cexpr` did not read the
// marker at all: a provide method compared an int against a float un-widened
// while the same expression in a `fn` was widened.
//
// Both operand orders and `!=` are here, so a one-sided fix cannot pass. The
// document is also the byte-parity oracle for the native chain, which is why
// the self-host lowering must stamp the same marker on the same operand.
//
// It sits in `tests/noncensus_corpus/` on purpose: this is an emitter-oracle
// document that reaches one reference branch, not a scoring or breadth
// program. Keeping it outside the census directories leaves the committed
// census program set (and its per-generation independence floors) unchanged;
// the emitter oracles list it in their CORPUS explicitly.
service Scores {
  fn above(x: Int) -> Bool
  fn below(x: Int) -> Bool
  fn differs(x: Int) -> Bool
}

component Judge provides scores: Scores {
  provide scores {
    fn above(x) = x == 4.0
    fn below(x) = 4.0 == x
    fn differs(x) = x != 4.0
  }
}
